    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nRight now the api is a bit inflexible in a few ways\r\n- left, right are mutually exclusive\r\n- outer and inner are mutually exclusive (can be fixed by defining the textobject spec with both inner and outer together, which brings me to the next problem:)\r\n- it can only use predefined specs, even though the specs I might want for movement may be different from the ones I want for selection\r\n\r\nI've been trying to tweak my jump mappings in a way that I find convenient and intuitive (not so much thinking about do I want to get to the end, or the beginning, including the current object or not, etc). And I think something like `]f` moving between both the outer beginning, inner beginning, inner end, outer end of functions, along with easy repeatability (hydra.nvim <3), seems ideal, would have to try but mini.ai doesn't support it for now.",
