            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for suggestion!\r\n\r\nI am not really sure what you want to achieve, to be honest. Maybe you could an example: text with cursor position and how pressing certain keys will work?\r\n\r\nMy best guess right now is that you want something like `]f` to cycle through four positions: right `i`, right `a`, left `a`, left `i`. If that is the case, this functionality is supported in 'mini.surround' with `sf` and `sF`. And both of them are dot-repeatable.",
