        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Surrounds find does cycle through those positions but it doesn't move to the next object after that (i'd have to use sfn, sfl, sFn, sFl which returns me to the problem of having too many different keybindings) so it doesn't exactly fit my needs, which is more about navigating across the whole codebase somewhat semantically. It should move between `{right, left} x {i, a} x {all instances of that text object}`, surround misses the last part of that product, ai misses the first two\r\n\r\nIt also has the problem of not being invokable from custom mappings, ie I don't know what i'd put as the rhs inside a hydra.nvim head to invoke find next with a specific textobject/surround, since i'd rather use that than . for repeating",
